Usage: chmod [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Change the mode of each FILE to MODE.

Each MODE is of the form '[ugoa]*([-+=]([rwxXst]*|[ugo]))+'.

  -H  traverse command-line symlinks to directories
  -L  traverse every symlink to a directory
  -P  do not traverse any symbolic links (default)

Note: On Windows, this command simulates Unix permissions using
file attributes. Write permission is mapped to the read-only attribute.

OPTIONS:
  -c, --changes           like verbose but report only when a change is made
  -f, --silent            suppress most error messages
  -v, --verbose           output a diagnostic for every file processed
  -R, --recursive         change files and directories recursively
      --quiet             suppress most error messages
      --reference ARG     use RFILE's mode instead of MODE values
  -H                      traverse command-line symlinks to directories
  -L                      traverse every symlink to a directory
  -P                      do not traverse any symbolic links (default)
      --dereference       affect the referent of each symbolic link
  -h, --no-dereference    affect symbolic links instead of referenced files
      --preserve-root     fail to operate recursively on '/'
      --no-preserve-root  do not treat '/' specially
      --help              display this help and exit
  -V, --version           output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
